      "locators": "Printed 6, 7–8, 10–11 and 18; Figures 1A, 4 and 6",
      "assessment": "E. coli YihU is a tetramer/dimer of dimers in crystal and solution. Kinetics used racemic SLA and assumed only D-SLA active; this relative label is not equated to absolute R. Original Figure 1A explicitly shows S-SLA and S-DHPS, supporting selected current absolute forms. Native old R comment is preserved as disagreement, not accepted."
    },
    {
      "source": "DOI:10.1021/acscentsci.0c01285.s001",
      "path": "/private/tmp/pathwaymech-next-201-evidence/sulfoquinovose/Sharma2021-SI-figshare.pdf",
      "sha256": "a4d4f57a30c7ac7cff3a62d644e074913ebda0390a5e0a91f91e5e97f560ffbc",
      "locators": "S10 Figure S9; S19 Figure S19; S20 Figure S20B; S30 sequences; S33–S34 kinetics",
      "assessment": "EcYihV dimer dominates with minor tetramer; SeYihT solution tetramer is not recast as Ec solution result. Both species have crystallographic tetramers in Figure S20. Fixed 10 mM additive effects remain condition scoped; Mg is not inferred solely from assay recipe."
    },
    {
